.TH "SIDE-DOG-BOARD" "1" "September 8, 2026" "Side Dog" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
\&side\-dog\-board \- coding\-agent activity viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS AND OPTIONS
.nf
\&side\-dog board [options]
\&List every coding\-agent session on the machine with its surface (Herdr pane,
\&  desktop app, editor, terminal), repository, branch, pull request, and
\&  status. Folders are discovered wherever agents are working; the watch
\&  folder cap does not apply.
\&
\&\-h, \-\-help
\&  show this help message and exit
\&
\&\-\-width WIDTH
\&  render width; 0 uses the full terminal pane
\&
\&\-\-poll POLL
\&  refresh interval in seconds
\&
\&\-\-github\-poll GITHUB_POLL
\&  minimum seconds between GitHub PR readbacks per folder; idle and finished
\&  branches back off automatically; 0 disables
\&
\&\-\-group {none,surface,repo}
\&  group rows under a header per repository (the default) or surface;
\&  overrides `group` in the [board] configuration table
\&
\&\-\-once
\&  print one frame and exit instead of staying on screen
\&
\&\-\-no\-detail
\&  start with the detail pane hidden; `d` or enter toggles it; overrides
\&  `detail` in the [board] configuration table
\&
\&\-\-no\-notify
\&  do not send desktop notifications for board changes such as a pull request
\&  going green while its session idles
\&
\&\-\-activity
\&  show recorded contributions by model/session over the last 24 hours
\&
\&FOLDER ([FOLDER ...])
\&  scope activity history to these folders; defaults to all saved folders
\&
\&\-\-no\-color
\&
.fi
.SH FIRST RUN
.nf
\&side\-dog \-\-version
\&side\-dog demo \-\-watch
\&side\-dog doctor .
\&side\-dog watch .
.fi
.SH VIEWS
Watch is chronological. Press b for Board contributions, a for its live
roster, and w to return.
Board --activity groups recorded work by repository, issue/PR, session and
event-time model over the last 24 hours.
Use j/k to select work and o to open its link. Completed contributors remain
in recorded history.
Unknown attribution is explicit. GitHub polling is an observation, never model
effort.
Only unambiguous recorded turn references link work; ambiguous actions remain
unlinked.
.SH FILES
~/.config/side-dog/config.toml: hand-authored configuration.
.br
~/.config/side-dog/spaces.toml: saved spaces, rewritten by watch --save.
.br
~/.local/state/side-dog/: disposable validated activity and display state.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
XDG_CONFIG_HOME overrides the configuration parent. SIDE_DOG_STATE_DIR
overrides runtime state.
.SH PRIVACY
Only validated metadata is persisted or exposed; never prompts, responses,
full commands, output, diffs or file contents.
Usage estimates are not allocated to PRs.
.SH SEE ALSO
side-dog(1), side-dog-watch(1), side-dog-board(1), side-dog-doctor(1)
.br
https://qfennessy.github.io/side-dog/
